G3307.def:
**μερίζω**
(μέρος), [in LXX chiefly for חָלַק ;]
**to divide**;
(a) **to divide into parts **: metaphorically, pass., [[1Co.7.34|1Co.7:34]] (WH, R, ing.), [[1Co.7.34|1Co.7:34]] (Rec., R, txt.) ( reading and punctuation, see _ICC_, in l); μεμέρισται ὁ Χριστός, [[1Co.1.13|1Co.1:13]] as in late authors, of factional division (cf. Polyb., viii, 23, 9), καθ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[Mat.12.25|Mat.12:25]] ἐφ᾽ εαυτόν, [[Mat.12.26|Mat.12:26]], [[Mrk.3.24-26|Mrk.3:24-26]];
(b) **to distribute**: with accusative of thing(s) and dative of person(s), [[Mrk.6.41|Mrk.6:41]] as in later usage (cf. Polyb., xi, 28, 9), **to bestow**: [[Rom.12.3|Rom.12:3]], [[1Co.7.17|1Co.7:17]], [[2Co.10.13|2Co.10:13]], [[Heb.7.2|Heb.7:2]]; mid., with accusative of thing(s) before μετά, [[Luk.12.13|Luk.12:13]] (cf. δια-, συμ-μερίζω).†
(AS)

G3392.def:
**μιαίνω **
[in LXX chiefly for טָמֵא ;]
1. to dye or stain.
2. **to stain, defile, soil**;
(a) **in physical sense**;
(b) **in moral sense **: [[Tit.1.15|Tit.1:15]], [[Heb.12.15|Heb.12:15]], [[Jude.8|Ju 8]];
(with) in ritual sense (cf. [[Lev.22.5|Lev.22:5]], al.): [[Jhn.18.28|Jhn.18:28]].†
_SYN._: μολύνω, to besmear, which also differs from μ. in that it is never used, as μ. in its primary meaning, in an honourable sense (cf. Tr., _Syn._, § xxxi) (AS)
